        "content": "## 🧪 TESTING GUIDE\n\n**Step 1: Activate Workflow**\n- Click \"Activate\" toggle (top-right)\n- Webhook URL will appear in Webhook Trigger node\n\n**Step 2: Get Webhook URL**\n- Click \"Webhook Trigger\" node\n- Copy the Production URL (e.g., https://your-n8n.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/startup-ceo-simulator)\n\n**Step 3: Test with cURL**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://your-n8n.app.n8n.cloud/webhook/startup-ceo-simulator \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"startupIdea\": \"An AI-powered platform that turns meeting transcripts into automated Jira tickets\"}'\n```\n\n**Step 4: Test with Postman**\n- Method: POST\n- URL: [your webhook URL]\n- Headers: Content-Type = application/json\n- Body (raw JSON):\n```json\n{\n  \"startupIdea\": \"An AI-powered platform that turns meeting transcripts into automated Jira tickets\"\n}\n```\n\n**Step 5: Monitor Execution**\n- Go to \"Executions\" tab (left sidebar)\n- Click latest execution to see:\n  - Each agent's analysis\n  - Synthesis output\n  - Generated artifacts\n\n**Expected Response Time:** 30-60 seconds\n\n**Success Indicators:**\n✅ All 4 agents return different perspectives\n✅ Synthesis identifies conflicts\n✅ 3 artifacts generated (pitch deck, roadmap, budget)\n✅ Final JSON contains all 9 fields",
